 concentration of anchor boxes used in object detection, which influences localization accuracy.'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'Localization Accuracy': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ["The precision with which an object's location is determined within an image."], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'Car detection': {'type': ['task'], 'description': ['The task of identifying and locating cars within images.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'Input image resolution': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['The size of the input images, which impacts the accuracy of car detection.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'Context window': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['An additional feature extraction method used to improve accuracy.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'Anchor box selection schemes': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['Different methods for selecting anchor boxes in Faster R-CNN.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'Inference time': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['The time taken by a model to make a prediction.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'Accuracy Difference': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['The percentage-point differences in accuracy observed when comparing R-CNN models with different convolutional layers (conv4_3 vs. conv5_3) of VGG16. Specifically, the accuracy is higher with conv4_3 by 5.5, 9.4, and 12.4 percentage-points for easy, medium, and hard detections, respectively.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'Inference Time AlexNet': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['The inference time using AlexNet conv5 layer with input image size of 5000 x 1510, which is 0.34 seconds.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'Inference Time VGG16': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['The inference time using VGG16 conv4_3 layer with input image size of 2000 x 604, which is 0.6 seconds.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, '3DOP': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A method mentioned for comparison of inference time on the KITTI dataset.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'Conv 4 3 Accuracy Values (Table 2)': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['The specific accuracy values for easy, medium, and hard detections when using VGG16 conv4_3, as presented in Table 2. The text mentions accuracy is higher by 5.5, 9.4, and 12.4 percentage points, but the exact values are missing.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'Conv 5 3 Accuracy Values (Table 2)': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['The specific accuracy values for easy, medium, and hard detections when using VGG16 conv5_3, as presented in Table 2. The text mentions that the accuracy is higher with conv4_3, but the exact values are missing.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'AlexNet Accuracy Values (Table 2)': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['The specific accuracy values for easy, medium, and hard detections when using AlexNet, as presented in Table 2. The text mentions the comparison with VGG16, but the exact values are missing.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'Context Window Accuracy Improvement (Table 4)': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['The specific accuracy improvements for all categories when applying the context window to an AlexNet-based R-CNN configuration, as shown in Table 4. The text states that the accuracy improves, but the exact values are missing.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'Fast R-CNN': {'description': ['An improved version of R-CNN that reuses shared convolution features for region proposals, aiming for faster inference.', 'A method that uses a region proposal network (RPN) to regress proposal boxes to ground truth boxes, improving upon Fast R-CNN.', 'An algorithm for object detection, used in the study and adapted for the KITTI dataset.', 'An improved version of R-CNN, incorporating a region proposal network.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 1, 2]}, 'Region Proposal Network (RPN)': {'description': ['A neural network that proposes regions of an image that are likely to contain objects. It is used in Faster R-CNN to improve the speed of object detection by replacing the selective search method.', 'A network used to propose regions of interest in an image.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 2]}, 'Convolutional layers': {'description': ['Layers within the neural networks (VGG16, AlexNet) used for feature extraction.', 'Layers within the AlexNet architecture. The text mentions that AlexNet has five convolutional layers, but does not specify which ones.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'conv5_3': {'description': ['Specific layer within the VGG16 architecture. It is the conv5_3 activation layer, which serves as input to both the region proposal network (RPN) and the classification network.', 'A specific layer within the VGG16 architecture (13th layer).', 'The 5th convolutional layer of AlexNet, used for feature extraction.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [1, 2]}}
